**Given:**

A can do a piece of work in 28 days.

B is 68% more efficient than A.

**Formula used:**

Efficiency is inversely proportional to the number of days taken to complete the work.

**Calculation:**

Let efficiency of A = 100 units

⇒ Efficiency of B = 168 units

Work done by A in 1 day = dfrac{1}{28}

⇒ Work done by B in 1 day = dfrac{1}{28} times dfrac{168}{100}

⇒ Work done by B in 1 day = dfrac{168}{2800} = dfrac{3}{50}

⇒ Number of days taken by B = dfrac{1}{dfrac{3}{50}}

⇒ Number of days taken by B = dfrac{50}{3}

**∴ The correct answer is option 3.**

**Given:**

First 17 natural numbers

**Formula used:**

Average of squares of first n natural numbers = dfrac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6n}

**Calculation:**

n = 17

⇒ dfrac{17(17+1)(2×17+1)}{6×17}

⇒ dfrac{17×18×35}{102}

⇒ dfrac{10710}{102}

⇒ 105

**∴ The correct answer is 105.**
